{
  "version": 2,
  "hash": "9690575560f6c29fd9e19498c1994541",
  "file_hash": "9690575560f6c29fd9e19498c1994541",
  "translated_at": "2026-11-10T05:10:25.420195",
  "target_lang": "en",
  "chunks": [
    {
      "hash": "dfe9992f585cafadc54def56669232c5",
      "translation": "# OneBot12 Platform Feature Documentation\n\nOneBot12Adapter is an adapter built based on the OneBot V12 protocol, serving as the baseline protocol adapter for the ErisPulse framework.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "hash": "cc76803739f9a0eedaddfd8fd8d95738",
      "translation": "## Document Information\n\n- Corresponding Module Version: 4.6.2\n- Maintainer: ErisPulse\n- Protocol Version: OneBot V12\n- Last Updated: 2026-11-10"
    },
    {
      "hash": "7cb073c9fc9ab7b7662e50a0ec987111",
      "translation": "## Basic Information\n\n- Platform Introduction: OneBot V12 is a general chatbot application interface standard and serves as the baseline protocol for the ErisPulse framework.\n- Adapter Name: OneBot12Adapter\n- Supported Protocol/API Version: OneBot V12\n- Multi-Account Support: Fully multi-account architecture, supporting simultaneous configuration and operation of multiple OneBot12 accounts."
    },
    {
      "hash": "e975e86e4706af5dc8f846f355d38ce5",
      "translation": "## v5 Paradigm Update (4.3.0)\n\nThis adapter has completed alignment with the v5 paradigm (incremental upgrade, API compatible):\n\n- **BaseConverter Inheritance**: Common fields of converters (id/time/platform/self/raw) are built by the framework's build_base_event, and are overridden by OB11 field names (echo/time/self_id).\n- **spawn_background Task Ownership**: Client mode connection tasks are now using Runtime.spawn_background (ownership assigned, shutdown automatically recycles).\n- **Framework Soft Dependency**: The adapter no longer declares a hard dependency on ErisPulse, avoiding pip resolution issues when adjusting framework versions; runtime detection ensures ErisPulse>=2.7.1, and logs a warning if the version is too low.\n- **Startup Version Log**: Outputs \"OneBot12Adapter vX.Y.Z loaded\" during initialization.\n\nExisting capabilities (supported since 4.2.0): Multi-account, standard action mapping for Api DSL (get_self_info→get_login_info, etc.), Request DSL (friend/group request approval: event.approve() / event.reject()), EventMixin, i18n."
    },
    {
      "hash": "4e1b99b4493416d15b73d4754bca24d8",
      "translation": "## Standardized Alignment\n\nThis section describes the behaviors of the adapter that align with the ErisPulse standardization specification. For details, refer to the SDK documentation:《Request Operation Specification》(`docs/en/standards/request-action-spec.md`) and《API Response Specification》(`docs/en/standards/api-response.md`).\n\n### Request Events and Request DSL\n\n- **request_id Guarantee**: When request events are forwarded, the top-level `request_id` field is guaranteed (prioritizing the native `request_id`, falling back to mapping the `flag` field for OB11-style implementations; synthesizing if neither is present), for use by Request DSL\n- **Default Account Fallback**: When `Request` DSL (based on the `handle_quick_request` action) does not explicitly specify an account via `Using()`, it falls back to using the source account of the request event (`request_context`), ensuring correct routing of `event.approve()`/`event.reject()` within the event chain\n\n### call_api Error Handling\n\n- When an account is not connected or the connection is closed, `call_api` no longer throws a `ConnectionError`, but instead returns a standard failure response (`status=\"failed\"`, `retcode=33001`)\n- API calls that timeout also return a standard failure response (`retcode=33001`)\n\n### Dual Compatibility of Account Fields and send_context\n\n- `call_api` accepts both the standard field `account_id` and the legacy field `_account_id` (with the standard name taking precedence); the framework's ApiDSL automatically adapts, and module code is recommended to use `account_id`\n- `Send`/`Recall`/`Edit`/`Batch` all methods read `send_context`: within the event chain, the account of the current event source is automatically used, with an explicitly specified account via `Using()` taking precedence\n\n### Event Field Injection\n\n- All events inject `self.account_id` (source account name), ensuring correct routing back to the source account in multi-account mode\n- All events must contain the `onebot12_raw_type` field (original event type, conforming to event transformation specifications)\n- Emoticon/pack/sticker message segments are named `onebot12_sticker` (sent internally via the `.Sticker()` method)\n\n### Error Code Specification\n\n| retcode | Meaning | Triggering Scenario |\n|---------|---------|---------------------|\n| 0 | Success | Action executed successfully |\n| 33001 | Network Error | Account not connected, connection closed, API call timeout |\n| 10002 | Unsupported Action | Backend does not support the requested action |\n| 10003 | Parameter Error | Missing necessary parameters |\n\n> The original response data returned by the backend is preserved in the `onebot12_raw` field."
    },
    {
      "hash": "5a00d5e09ab0097710fb705690c0f14b",
      "translation": "## Standard API Actions (Api DSL)\n\nThe OneBot12 backend natively supports all OB12 standard action names. The Api DSL defaults to directly delegating call_api for transparent transmission (no mapping required):\n\n```python\nfrom ErisPulse import sdk\nob12 = sdk.adapter.get(\"onebot12\")\n\nresult = await ob12.Api.get_self_info()\nresult = await ob12.Api.get_friend_list()\nawait ob12.Api.delete_message(message_id=\"MSG_ID\")\n\n# Specify account (multi-account)\nresult = await ob12.Api.Using(\"main\").get_self_info()\n\n# Platform extension actions\nresult = await ob12.Api.call(\"extend_action\", param=1)\n```\n\n> Supported actions are based on the backend implementation (e.g., NapCat/Lagrange/LLOneBot); unsupported actions return errors from the backend and are transparently passed through.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "hash": "7c3ee066adcc659888f7edfaccfdeb94",
      "translation": "## Request Operations (Request DSL)\n\nBased on the OneBot12 standard handle_quick_request action, handles approval/rejection of friend requests and group invitation requests:\n\n### Event Convenience Methods\n\n```python\nfrom ErisPulse.Core.Event import request\n\n@request.on_friend_request()\nasync def handle_friend_request(event):\n    if event.get(\"platform\") != \"onebot12\":\n        return\n    comment = event.get(\"comment\", \"\")\n    if comment == \"passphrase\":\n        await event.approve()      # Approve\n    else:\n        await event.reject()       # Reject\n```\n\n### Manual Request DSL Calls\n\n```python\nawait ob12.Request(\"request_flag\").accept()\nawait ob12.Request(\"request_flag\").reject()\nawait ob12.Request(\"request_flag\").Using(\"main\").accept()\n```\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "hash": "126b42528412c7c51fe050af83b15307",
      "translation": "## Supported Message Sending Types\n\nAll sending methods are implemented using a fluent interface syntax, for example:\n\n```python\nfrom ErisPulse.Core import adapter\nonebot12 = adapter.get(\"onebot12\")\n\n# Send using the default account\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", group_id).Text(\"Hello World!\")\n\n# Send using a specific account\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", group_id).Account(\"main\").Text(\"Message from main account\")\n```\n\n### Case-Insensitive Method Calls\n\nAll sending methods and fluent modifier methods support case-insensitive calls, and the adapter automatically maps them to the correct standard method names:\n\n```python\n# All the following calls are equivalent\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"user\", 123).Text(\"hello\")\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"user\", 123).text(\"hello\")\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"user\", 123).TEXT(\"hello\")\n\n# Fluent modifier methods also support this\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", 123).At(456).Text(\"hello\")\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", 123).at(456).TEXT(\"hello\")\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", 123).AT(456).text(\"hello\")\n```\n\n### Unsupported Method Calls\n\nWhen calling an unsupported method, the adapter returns a friendly text message instead of raising an exception:\n\n```python\n# Calling an unsupported method\nresult = await onebot12.Send.To(\"user\", 123).UnsupportedMethod(\"test\")\n\n# The returned result is a text message\n# Message content: [Unsupported sending type] Method name: UnsupportedMethod, Parameters: [args[0]: 'test']\n```\n\n### Basic Message Types\n\n- `.Text(text: str)` : Send plain text messages\n- `.Image(file: Union[str, bytes], filename: str = \"image.png\")` : Send image messages (supports URL, Base64, or bytes)\n- `.Audio(file: Union[str, bytes], filename: str = \"audio.ogg\")` : Send audio messages\n- `.Voice(file: Union[str, bytes], filename: str = \"voice.ogg\")` : Send voice messages (an alias of Audio, compatible with OneBot11)\n- `.Video(file: Union[str, bytes], filename: str = \"video.mp4\")` : Send video messages\n\n### Fluent Modifier Methods (return self to support fluent chaining)\n\n- `.At(user_id: Union[str, int])` : @ user (can be called multiple times)\n- `.AtAll()` : @ all members\n- `.Reply(message_id: Union[str, int])` : Reply to a message\n\n### Raw Message Sending\n\n- `.Raw_ob12(message: Union[Dict, List[Dict]], **kwargs)` : Send OneBot12 raw format messages (conforms to naming conventions)\n\n### Other Message Types\n\n- `.Sticker(file_id: str)` : Send sticker/emoticon messages (`onebot12_sticker` message segment)\n- `.Location(latitude: float, longitude: float, title: str = \"\", content: str = \"\")` : Send location messages\n\n### Management Features\n\n- `.Recall(message_id: Union[str, int])` : Recall a message\n- `.Edit(message_id: Union[str, int], content: Union[str, List[Dict]])` : Edit a message\n- `.Raw(message_segments: List[Dict])` : Send native OneBot12 message segments\n- `.Batch(target_ids: List[str], message: Union[str, List[Dict]], target_type: str = \"user\")` : Batch send messages"
    },
    {
      "hash": "f7bc92585b4e7c862540ff0c22a23954",
      "translation": "## OneBot12 Standard Events\n\nThe OneBot12 adapter fully complies with the OneBot12 standard, and event formats do not require conversion, being directly submitted to the framework.\n\n### New Feature: Raw Event Type Field\n\nCompliant with the `standards/event-conversion.md` specification, all events will retain the raw event type field `onebot12_raw_type`:\n\n```python\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"message\",              # Event type\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"message\", # Raw event type (same as type)\n    \"detail_type\": \"private\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"message\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"Hello\"}}],\n    \"alt_message\": \"Hello\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n```\n\n### Message Events\n\n```python\n# Private message\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"message\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"private\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"message\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"Hello\"}}],\n    \"alt_message\": \"Hello\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n\n# Group message\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"message\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"group\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"group_id\": \"group-id\",\n    \"message\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"Hello group\"}}],\n    \"alt_message\": \"Hello group\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n```\n\n### Notice Events\n\n```python\n# Group member increase\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"notice\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"notice\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"group_member_increase\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"group_id\": \"group-id\",\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"operator_id\": \"operator-id\",\n    \"sub_type\": \"approve\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n\n# Group member decrease\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"notice\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"notice\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"group_member_decrease\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"group_id\": \"group-id\",\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"operator_id\": \"operator-id\",\n    \"sub_type\": \"leave\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n```\n\n### Request Events\n\n```python\n# Friend request\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"request\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"request\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"friend\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"comment\": \"Application message\",\n    \"request_id\": \"request-flag\",\n    \"flag\": \"request-flag\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n\n# Group invitation request\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"request\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"request\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"group\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"group_id\": \"group-id\",\n    \"user_id\": \"user-id\",\n    \"comment\": \"Application message\",\n    \"request_id\": \"request-flag\",\n    \"flag\": \"request-flag\",\n    \"sub_type\": \"invite\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n```\n\n### Meta Events\n\n```python\n# Lifecycle event\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"meta_event\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"meta_event\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"lifecycle\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"sub_type\": \"enable\",\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n\n// Heartbeat event\n{\n    \"id\": \"event-id\",\n    \"type\": \"meta_event\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"meta_event\",\n    \"detail_type\": \"heartbeat\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"bot-id\"},\n    \"interval\": 5000,\n    \"status\": {\"online\": true},\n    \"time\": 1234567890\n}\n```"
    },
    {
      "hash": "9ebcadf6d3ed5ed4e2843bf137c0ab97",
      "translation": "## Configuration Options\n\n### Account Configuration\n\nEach account independently configures the following options:\n\n- `mode`: The running mode of this account (\"server\" or \"client\")\n- `server_path`: WebSocket path in Server mode\n- `server_token`: Authentication token in Server mode (optional)\n- `client_url`: WebSocket address to connect in Client mode\n- `client_token`: Authentication token in Client mode (optional)\n- `enabled`: Whether to enable this account\n- `platform`: Platform identifier, default is \"onebot12\"\n- `implementation`: Implementation identifier, such as \"go-cqhttp\" (optional)\n\n### Configuration Example\n\n```toml\n[OneBotv12_Adapter.accounts.main]\nmode = \"server\"\nserver_path = \"/onebot12-main\"\nserver_token = \"main_token\"\nenabled = true\nplatform = \"onebot12\"\nimplementation = \"go-cqhttp\"\n\n[OneBotv12_Adapter.accounts.backup]\nmode = \"client\"\nclient_url = \"ws://127.0.0.1:3002\"\nclient_token = \"backup_token\"\nenabled = true\nplatform = \"onebot12\"\nimplementation = \"shinonome\"\n\n[OneBotv12_Adapter.accounts.test]\nmode = \"client\"\nclient_url = \"ws://127.0.0.1:3003\"\nenabled = false\n```\n\n### Default Configuration\n\nIf no account is configured, the adapter will automatically create:\n\n```toml\n[OneBotv12_Adapter.accounts.default]\nmode = \"server\"\nserver_path = \"/onebot12\"\nenabled = true\nplatform = \"onebot12\"\n```"
    },
    {
      "hash": "f25fc81f88aa05438a22815ed9f13cc6",
      "translation": "## Send Method Return Values\n\n### Message Sending Methods\nAll message sending methods (such as `.Text()`, `.Image()`, `.Raw_ob12()`, etc.) return an `asyncio.Task` object, which can be directly awaited to get the sending result:\n\n```python\ntask = await onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", 123456).Text(\"Hello\")\n```\n\n### Chain Modifier Methods\nAll chain modifier methods (such as `.At()`, `.AtAll()`, `.Reply()`) return `self`, supporting chain calls:\n\n```python\n# Combine multiple modifier methods\nawait onebot12.Send.To(\"group\", 123456).Reply(\"msg123\").At(789).At(790).Text(\"text\")\n```"
    },
    {
      "hash": "14a9a91b885b0ff3a4045ebce366e1a1",
      "translation": "## API Response Standard\n\nThe adapter follows the ErisPulse standardized return specification (`standards/api-response.md`):\n\n```python\n# Success response\n{\n    \"status\": \"ok\",              // Required: execution status\n    \"retcode\": 0,                // Required: return code (0 indicates success)\n    \"data\": {                     // Required: response data\n        \"message_id\": \"123456\",\n        \"time\": 1632847927.599013\n    },\n    \"message_id\": \"123456\",       // Required: message ID (empty string if none)\n    \"message\": \"\",                // Required: error message (empty if successful)\n    \"echo\": \"1234\",               // Optional: echo returned as-is from the request\n    \"onebot12_raw\": {...}        // Optional: raw response data\n}\n\n# Failure response\n{\n    \"status\": \"failed\",           // Required: execution status\n    \"retcode\": 10003,            // Required: return code (non-zero indicates failure)\n    \"data\": None,                // Required: null on failure\n    \"message_id\": \"\",            // Required: empty string on failure\n    \"message\": \"Missing required parameter\",    // Required: error description\n    \"echo\": \"1234\",              // Optional: echo returned as-is from the request\n    \"onebot12_raw\": {...}        // Optional: raw response data\n}\n```\n\n### Error Code Specification\n\nFollows OneBot12 standard error codes:\n\n- **0**: Success\n- **1xxxx**: Action request error\n- **2xxxx**: Action handler error\n- **3xxxx**: Action execution error (33001 for network timeout)\n\n### Multi-Account Sending Syntax\n\n```python\n# Account selection methods\nawait onebot12.Send.Using(\"main\").To(\"group\", 123456).Text(\"Main account message\")\nawait onebot12.Send.Using(\"backup\").To(\"group\", 123456).Image(\"http://example.com/image.jpg\")\n\n# API call method\nawait onebot12.call_api(\"send_message\", account_id=\"main\", \n    detail_type=\"group\", group_id=123456, \n    content=[{\"type\": \"text\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"Hello\"}}])\n```"
    },
    {
      "hash": "ab72ae00c4d2c4acd22f0845c103dd10",
      "translation": "## Asynchronous Processing Mechanism\n\nThe OneBot12 adapter uses an asynchronous non-blocking design:\n\n1. Message sending does not block the event handling loop.\n2. Multiple concurrent sending operations can be performed simultaneously.\n3. API responses are handled promptly.\n4. WebSocket connections remain active.\n5. Multi-account concurrent processing, with each account running independently."
    },
    {
      "hash": "b0f390ddfca9494ed1daecec22a9b681",
      "translation": "## Error Handling\n\nThe adapter provides a comprehensive error handling mechanism:\n\n1. Automatic reconnection for network connection exceptions (supports independent reconnection for each account, with a 30-second interval)\n2. API call timeout handling (fixed 30-second timeout; timeout returns the standard failure response `retcode=33001`)\n3. When an account is not connected or the connection is closed, `call_api` returns the standard failure response `retcode=33001` instead of throwing a `ConnectionError`\n4. Calling unsupported methods will return a friendly text prompt"
    },
    {
      "hash": "32f725df7ae57d967a2837a82f1905ce",
      "translation": "## Event Handling Enhancement\n\nIn multi-account mode, all events are automatically appended with account information:\n\n```python\n{\n    \"type\": \"message\",\n    \"onebot12_raw_type\": \"message\",  // Raw event type\n    \"detail_type\": \"private\",\n    \"self\": {\"user_id\": \"123456\"},  // Account ID that sent the event (standard field)\n    \"platform\": \"onebot12\",\n    // ... other event fields\n}\n```"
    },
    {
      "hash": "86fbd72fe4f9e8954db5d1b78a5462bd",
      "translation": "## Management Interface\n\n```python\n# Get all account information\naccounts = onebot12.accounts\n\n# Check account connection status\nconnection_status = {\n    account_id: connection is not None and not connection.closed\n    for account_id, connection in onebot12.connections.items()\n}\n\n# Dynamically enable/disable accounts (requires adapter restart)\nonebot12.accounts[\"test\"].enabled = False\n```"
    },
    {
      "hash": "551df13034fb0864d09f3749235ed15d",
      "translation": "## OneBot12 Standard Features\n\n### Message Segment Standard\n\nOneBot12 uses standardized message segment formats:\n\n```python\n# Text message segment\n{\"type\": \"text\", \"data\": {\"text\": \"Hello\"}}\n\n# Image message segment\n{\"type\": \"image\", \"data\": {\"file_id\": \"image-id\"}}\n\n# Mention message segment\n{\"type\": \"mention\", \"data\": {\"user_id\": \"user-id\", \"user_name\": \"Username\"}}\n\n# Reply message segment\n{\"type\": \"reply\", \"data\": {\"message_id\": \"msg-id\"}}\n```\n\n### API Standard\n\nFollows OneBot12 standard API specifications:\n\n- `send_message`: Send message\n- `delete_message`: Recall message\n- `edit_message`: Edit message\n- `get_message`: Get message\n- `get_self_info`: Get self information\n- `get_user_info`: Get user information\n- `get_group_info`: Get group information"
    },
    {
      "hash": "249f0edde1119752d303d8f7f2bcf0b4",
      "translation": "## Best Practices\n\n1. **Configuration Management**: It is recommended to use multi-account configuration to separate management of robots with different purposes.\n2. **Error Handling**: Always check the return status of API calls.\n3. **Message Sending**: Use appropriate message types and avoid sending unsupported messages.\n4. **Connection Monitoring**: Regularly check connection status to ensure service availability.\n5. **Performance Optimization**: Use the Batch method for batch sending to reduce network overhead.\n6. **Method Calls**: Standard camelCase naming (e.g., `.Text()`) is recommended, but lowercase forms are also supported for compatibility with different programming styles (this may be incompatible with older versions)."
    }
  ]
}